#emph[Brihat Samhita] (Varahamihira) on planetary metallurgy -
#emph[Rasaratna Samuccaya] graha-rasa identifications - #emph[Charaka
Samhita] on therapeutic correspondences

Within the dhatu/jeeva/moola classification: - #strong[Chandra is
dhatu-graha] — the "structural/embodying" class - This places silver in
the same metaphysical category as Mangala (copper) and Shani (iron) —
substances that #emph[constitute] rather than #emph[animate]

The Chandra correspondence is internally consistent with multiple
classical claims: - #strong[Color match]: silver’s white luster
corresponds to lunar light - #strong[Cyclical responsiveness]: silver’s
tarnishing-and-cleaning cycle corresponds to lunar waxing-and-waning -
#strong[Cooling property]: silver is described as #emph[shita] (cool),
opposite of gold’s #emph[ushna] (warm); matches Chandra’s cooling tattva
- #strong[Manas (mind)]: Chandra rules the mind in jyotish; silver
preparations are classically indicated for #emph[manasika] (mental)
disorders, #emph[unmada] (psychosis), #emph[apasmara] (epilepsy) -
#strong[Receptivity]: Chandra is the most receptive graha (receives
Sun’s light, reflects to earth); silver is the most receptive metal to
