  [Multiple antimicrobial studies],
  [Various],
  [IC50 78.54 μg/ml against MCF-7 cancer cells; antibacterial against
  gram-pos and gram-neg],
)
]

#strong[Convergent finding]: traditional rajata-bhasma is #strong[silver
sulfide (Ag₂S, acanthite phase) at the nanoscale] with intermediate
Ag-Hg-S compounds present in incompletely processed batches. The final
product is NOT pure silver, unlike swarna-bhasma which IS pure gold.

This is consistent with silver chemistry: at the temperatures and
conditions of puta processing, silver reacts irreversibly with sulfur.
The tradition’s procedure produces what the chemistry permits — Ag₂S
nanoparticles, which have therapeutic activity in their own right.

#strong[Reproducibility:] High. The procedure is standardized; multiple
modern characterizations confirm consistent product chemistry.

