== 3. Major Silver Preparations
<major-silver-preparations>
=== 3.1 Rajata-Bhasma (Silver Calx / Silver Sulfide Nanoparticles)
<rajata-bhasma-silver-calx-silver-sulfide-nanoparticles>
#strong[Composition:] Ag₂S (acanthite, monoclinic) primarily; some
Ag-Hg-S intermediates in less-processed batches \
#strong[Color:] reddish-brown to dark brown (counterintuitive — pure
silver is silver-white, but Ag₂S nanoparticles are dark; the color shift
signals chemical conversion) \
#strong[Particle size:] 10-100 nm (nano-range), with some agglomeration
to 1-10 μm clusters \
#strong[Source text:] Rasaratna Samuccaya, Bhaishajya Ratnavali, Rasa
Tarangini

#strong[Therapeutic indications (classical):] - #emph[Manasika] (mental
disorders) - #emph[Apasmara] (epilepsy) - #emph[Unmada] (mania,
psychosis) - #emph[Hrid-roga] (heart disease) - #emph[Pradara]
(menorrhagia, leucorrhoea) - Indicated as #emph[hridya] (cardiotonic),
#emph[medhya] (intellect-supporting), #emph[rasayana] (rejuvenating),
#emph[vrishya] (aphrodisiac), #emph[vajikarana] (vitalizing)

#strong[Modern pharmacology research:] - Anti-cancer activity: IC50
78.54 μg/ml against MCF-7 breast cancer cell line (Chute et al.) -
Antimicrobial: confirmed against multiple bacterial species -
Anti-inflammatory effects documented - Cardioprotective effects in
preliminary studies - Cognitive-supportive effects under investigation

#strong[Dosage:] 30-125 mg twice daily classical; modern licensed
Ayurvedic practice typically 60-125 mg daily

#strong[Toxicity:] Silver in elemental form has very low toxicity
(silver is a safe noble metal). Ag₂S is similarly low-toxicity for
short-term use. #emph[Argyria] (skin discoloration from chronic silver
accumulation) is the main long-term concern with any silver preparation;
classical dosing at 30-125 mg/day is generally below the threshold for
argyria with short-term use, but chronic use over years can produce the
irreversible blue-grey skin pigmentation.

