=== 5.4 The empirical convergence finding
<the-empirical-convergence-finding>
Silver shows good but qualified empirical convergence between classical
claim and modern characterization. The texts said: - Silver reduced to
fine ash form ✓ - Particles able to enter finger furrows (≤10 μm) ✓
(1-100 nm with some agglomeration) - Surface tension permits floating on
water ✓ (sub-micron features) - No metallic shine when finely powdered ✓
(sub-wavelength particles) - Cannot be reverted to bulk silver by simple
heating ✓ (Ag₂S is stable)

Modern characterization confirms: - Predominantly Ag₂S, not metallic Ag
(the distinction the texts don’t make explicit) - Particle size 10-100
nm - Color shift to reddish-brown indicates conversion (sub-wavelength
particles) - Antibacterial and anti-cancer activity at therapeutic doses

The convergence is strong enough to support continued therapeutic use of
properly-prepared rajata-bhasma. The chemistry-clarification (Ag₂S vs
metallic Ag) is a refinement, not a refutation, of the classical
understanding.

