== 9. Closing Notes
<closing-notes>
Silver illustrates an important pattern: the same classical procedure
applied to two noble metals (gold and silver) produces chemically
different end products because the metals have different reactivities.
This is not a flaw in the procedure or the tradition — it is what the
chemistry permits. Gold remains pure Au; silver becomes Ag₂S. Both
bhasma forms are therapeutically active in their respective ways.

The framework predictions for silver operations are notably broader than
for other dhatus. Chandra’s no-enemy status across the BPHS friendship
matrix means silver operations have many favorable timing windows. This
matches actual practice: silver-bhasma is reliably produced year-round
in licensed pharmacies without strong timing-prescription, in contrast
to mercurial preparations which traditionally are scheduled with more
care.

The Pushya nakshatra finding continues to emerge across multi-graha
mercurial operations: Volume I (kajjali), Volume II (makaradhwaja), and
now Volume III (rajata-bhasma three-graha context). This is a derivable
framework prediction worth empirical testing through retrospective QC
analysis of licensed-pharmacy batches.

